4. PEAK INTERVAL
==============================================================================
(a) TIED MAXIMUM: z=1.54 at bins BCE [3300, 3200, 3100, 3000] -> interval 3300-3000 BCE (4 consecutive 100-yr bins)
    cultural periods of peak bins: ['MN']
    ordinal-millennium membership of peak bins: ['4th mill', '4th mill', '4th mill', '3rd mill']
    The maximum is TIED across bins: a single 'peak year' would be an artefact of
    interpolation, not a feature of the data.

(b) HIGHSTAND z>=1.46: BCE 4000-3000 (11 consecutive bins, z in [1.46,1.54]); periods ['EN', 'MN']
    next-highest value anywhere else in the series: z=0.37 (BCE 2900) -> the highstand is a clean, isolated plateau

(c) SMOOTHED MODE (Amber_inter sensitivity; annual values are interpolated):
     300-yr centred rolling mean: mode at 3150 BCE (z=1.540)
     500-yr centred rolling mean: mode at 3243 BCE (z=1.517)
    1000-yr centred rolling mean: mode at 3493 BCE (z=1.488)
    -> smoothed mode lies inside 3300-3000 BCE for windows <=500 yr; the 1000-yr window
       (too wide for a 39-point series) drags the mode early. Annual data cannot refine
       the peak below the 100-yr bin.

